Security Control Categories

Technical controls involve electronic computing systems like intrusion detection systems, antivirus, and firewalls that provide security.
Operational controls relate to how an organization operates structurally, including roles such as chief information security officer and data custodian.
Managerial and Physical Controls

Managerial controls are decisions made by managers on security practices, such as how often to recertify badges or change passwords.
Physical controls are tangible security measures like locked doors, security gates, and lighting that physically prevent unauthorized access.
Exam Tips on Security Controls

The exam will not require distinguishing between categories and types or memorizing lists; understanding concepts is more important.
Some controls may overlap categories (e.g., electronic badge readers), but exam questions will focus on clear examples like physical gates.
